# Better Auth with Next.js Integration

Based on the documentation, here's the essential setup:

## 1) Server Auth Instance (auth.ts)

The documentation doesn't provide a complete `betterAuth` config example with all those specific parameters. It only shows:

```ts
import { betterAuth } from "better-auth";
import { nextCookies } from "better-auth/next-js";

export const auth = betterAuth({
    // ...your config
    plugins: [nextCookies()]
})
```

You'll need to consult the installation guide for full configuration including `secret`, `baseURL`, `emailAndPassword`, and `socialProviders.google`.

## 2) API Route Handler (app router)

```ts title="api/auth/[...all]/route.ts"
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";
import { toNextJsHandler } from "better-auth/next-js";

export const { GET, POST } = toNextJsHandler(auth);
```

## 3) Client Auth Instance

```ts title="auth-client.ts"
import { createAuthClient } from "better-auth/react"

export const authClient = createAuthClient({
    // client configuration here
})
```

## 4) Server-Side Session Retrieval

```tsx title="app/dashboard/page.tsx"
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";
import { headers } from "next/headers";

export default async function DashboardPage() {
    const session = await auth.api.getSession({
        headers: await headers()
    })
    // Use session...
}
```

## 5) Route Protection Recommendation

The docs recommend: "in Next.js proxy/middleware, it's recommended to only check for the existence of a session cookie" for optimization, but also state that "you must always validate the session on your server for any protected actions or pages."

