# Better Auth Code Examples

## signUp.email
```ts
const { data, error } = await authClient.signUp.email({
    email,
    password,
    name,
    image,
    callbackURL: "/dashboard"
}, {
    onRequest: (ctx) => { /* show loading */ },
    onSuccess: (ctx) => { /* redirect after verification */ },
    onError: (ctx) => { alert(ctx.error.message); }
});
```

## signIn.email
```ts
const { data, error } = await authClient.signIn.email({
    email,
    password,
    callbackURL: "/dashboard",
    rememberMe: false
}, {
    onRequest: (ctx) => { /* show loading */ },
    onSuccess: (ctx) => { /* handle success */ },
    onError: (ctx) => { alert(ctx.error.message); }
});
```

## signIn.social (Google)
```ts
await authClient.signIn.social({
    provider: "github",
    callbackURL: "/dashboard",
    errorCallbackURL: "/error",
    newUserCallbackURL: "/welcome",
    disableRedirect: true
});
```

## signOut
```ts
await authClient.signOut({
    fetchOptions: {
        onSuccess: () => {
            router.push("/login");
        }
    }
});
```

## useSession (React)
```tsx
const { data: session, isPending, error, refetch } = authClient.useSession();
```

Per the documentation: "Always invoke client methods from the client side. Don't call them from the server."

